THE PAINTINGS

The MIT licence above covers the code in this repository. It does not cover the
paintings, and does not need to: works produced for the U.S. federal government
by its employees are not subject to copyright in the United States (17 U.S.C.
§ 105), and the National Agricultural Library publishes the USDA Pomological
Watercolor Collection as public domain.

Two files here contain reproductions of those paintings rather than code:

    docs/preview.jpg         six compositions, for the README
    prototypes/assets.json   plates inlined into the phone prototype

Everything else the tools produce is rendered on your own machine from scans
you download yourself; none of them are redistributed here.

NAL asks that use of the paintings carry the credit below. That is a request
rather than a licence condition, and this project honours it in the README, in
the generated preview image, and here:

  U.S. Department of Agriculture Pomological Watercolor Collection. Rare and
  Special Collections, National Agricultural Library, Beltsville, MD 20705.
